From ae40cbfccbebdad6eed639b385d7fffc8bc5cdba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:32:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the sent message stays pinned at the top, minimized
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.3 (ask 16), as the operator clarified it: as in
Cursor, once a message is sent it stays at the top of the thread,
minimized to one line, while the reply scrolls under it.

The rule is one function, pinned_user_message_ix, over the entry at
the viewport's top: the last user message above it is pinned, unless
the entry at the top is a user message itself -- whole or partly
scrolled past, it is on screen, and a pinned copy would sit over it.
So a newer message takes the place of an older one when its turn
scrolls under the top, and scrolling back up into an earlier turn pins
that turn's message: one sticky header per user message. Before the
first message nothing is pinned.

The header is an overlay at the top of the conversation, beside 0026's
floating navigation: a person icon, the message's first non-blank line
truncated, and a chevron. A click on the line jumps to the message
(scroll to its entry, offset 0), which hides the header; the chevron
expands the whole message in place, wrapped, scrolling past 160 px,
and points up to minimize it. Which message is expanded is kept by
entry index, so a different pinned message always arrives minimized.

The code lives in conversation_view/thread_view/pinned_message.rs; the
thread view gains one field and one child.

Tests: pinned_message::tests (the turn under the top pins its message;
a newer one takes its place; hidden while the message is on screen,
whole or partly; scrolling back up pins the earlier one; nothing
before the first message or past the end; the minimized line is the
first non-blank one). Seen failing with the on-screen rule removed and
with the rule answering None.
---

